# #vi-sysdiag-grid at scale — the real 21-card architecture (see .werk/diagram.mmd for the
# source Mermaid this was translated from), not the 4-card mv/cp/st/lv prototype.
#
# Two known losses in the translation, both worth recording on #vi-sysdiag-grid-gaps:
#   - Mermaid's three dotted edges (child->gate, gate->approvebar, log->tracker) become solid
#     here. The grid pipeline has no dashed-stroke option yet.
#   - `dev -->|reloads the server| proc` targeted a SUBGRAPH, not a card. A grid edge must
#     touch a card (R3), so it is retargeted to `runner` here.
#
# Third variant, from scratch, per #vi-sysdiag-grid-singlecell-scale: diagram-grid-full.wgrid
# gave every card 2 rows (bookkeeping only) and 3+ columns (padding around 1 real touch
# column). diagram-grid-full-flat.wgrid proved the 2nd row was dead weight. diagram-grid-
# full-flat-narrow.wgrid then deleted only the padding columns no edge anywhere ever touched
# — 8 of 39. That mechanical approach was exhausted: most of the remaining width came from the
# 2 long detour lanes (gate_approvebar, cli_log) eating columns other cards would otherwise
# give up, not from any card's own need.
#
# This file is authored from scratch instead: every card starts at 1 row x 1 column, and is
# widened only when it has more than 1 edge attaching from the SAME single direction (a single
# cell already has all 4 neighbours at once, so edges on different faces never force width).
# Counting from the edge list above:
#   - state:  4 columns — 3 edges arrive from the north (tree, detail, rollup); one north column is now unused; its
#     own south edge (to foldfn) reuses one of those 4 columns.
#   - live:   5 columns — 5 edges arrive from the north (approvebar, composer, transcript,
#     tabs, header); its own south edge (to runner) reuses one of those 5.
#   - runner: 3 columns — 3 edges leave south (to chatlog, lock, child); its north edge (from
#     live) and east edge (from dev) each reuse one of those 3 columns.
#   - child:  2 columns — 2 edges leave south (to gate, to cli), placed contiguously; its own
#     north edge (from runner) reuses one of the 2.
# Every other card, including gate and cli, stayed 1x1: gate receives child_gate from the
# north and gate_allow leaves south (1 each), and gate_approvebar is routed to touch gate's
# WEST face instead of north — a different face, so it adds no width. Symmetrically cli
# receives child_cli from the north, and cli_log is routed to touch cli's EAST face instead —
# again a different face. Both of gate/cli would have needed 2 columns had the detour lanes
# reused the same face as the existing fan-in edge; routing them to a free face instead is
# what keeps gate and cli at 1x1. (This corrects the task's own working guess that gate would
# need width — a smarter face assignment for the detour avoids it.)
#
# The 2 detours run in their own dedicated lane, never sharing a column with a card's own
# span:
#   - gate_approvebar: a single column (separate from every card's columns) running the full
#     height from approvebar's row down to gate's row, then a short 2-cell horizontal jog at
#     gate's own row to reach gate's west face.
#   - cli_log: a column just east of log, running down to the bottom row, a horizontal jog
#     along that otherwise-empty bottom row, then a second column just east of cli, running
#     back up to touch cli's east face. This is a genuine U-shape (down, across, back up), so
#     it still trips the same "U-shaped detour" warning the wider versions did — narrower
#     authored cells, not a straighter line.
#
# Every edge in the content section carries a label, and R4 requires a label to split its
# path into two pieces it bridges (never sit beside an unbroken path) — so every hop between
# two directly-connected card rows still costs the same 3 gap rows (path, label, path) as the
# earlier variants. Row count is therefore close to unchanged; only column width shrank.
#
# Added `diagram`, in MAP VIEW alongside tree/graph3d/detail/rollup: this picture drawn from
# this very file. It has no edges — the Diagram tab reads .werk/diagram-*.svg/wgrid straight
# off disk (server.ts's /api/diagram-svg, /api/diagram-source), not through GET /api/graph the
# way tree/detail/rollup do, so wiring it to `state` the way they are would be a false
# edge, not a simplification. What the addition actually cost: 1 line in the content section,
# and 1 new column, inserted once between rollup's column and the gate->approvebar lane and
# carried down every row (as `.`, except where a horizontal run — cli->log's bottom-row detour
# — was already crossing that exact point, where it had to extend through instead of getting
# cut in two). Placing `diagram` in that new column's row 0, next to rollup rather than off in
# some unrelated row, is what keeps MAP VIEW's own frame from stretching down into SERVER
# PROCESS's rows — the failure mode #vi-sysdiag-grid-groupshape wants a checker rule for.
#
# `child -->|writes the diagram source directly, no log entry| diagram` — #vi-sysdiag-grid-
# lanewall's edge, drawn for real. It is the one honest connection: unlike everything else
# here, which goes through `child -->|changes the map| cli -->|appends the change| log`, this
# file is edited directly by the agent, no log entry, no audit trail. Drawing it required two
# things, not one:
#   - Junction cells (#vi-sysdiag-grid-junction): a new `<edgeA>+<edgeB>` token where two
#     edges cross at one cell, each blind to the other, check.ts's R6. Necessary but not
#     sufficient — a junction only crosses a LONG edge with a real pass-through cell
#     (gate->approvebar, cli->log); a short 1-hop bridge edge (child->gate, child->cli,
#     runner->child, live->runner, dev->runner) has none, every one of its cells touches
#     either its card or its own label.
#   - Reordering runner's south fan. `child` used to be the fan member farthest from
#     gate->approvebar's lane (past chatlog and lock), which meant reaching it crossed not
#     just the lane but that whole cluster of uncrossable short edges. Moved `child` to be
#     the fan member NEXT to the lane instead (chatlog and lock shifted over), so the only
#     thing between column 4 (diagram's own clear column, and now child->diagram's own
#     vertical run) and `child` is gate->approvebar itself — one junction, at (row 12,
#     col 5), then a single plain cell into child's west face. live->runner and runner's own
#     card now also reuse child's column (8) as their through-line, so live -> runner ->
#     child sits on one straight vertical spine; chatlog and lock moved to columns 9 and 10,
#     gate and cli shifted 1 column left to stay under child->gate/child->cli, and
#     dev->runner's horizontal bridge shifted right to keep clear of the wider runner span.
#   Verified, not assumed: every original card and edge is still present (23 cards, 23 edges,
#   diffed by id against the pre-change set), 0 build errors, and the new edge's resolved path
#   was read back programmatically to confirm it actually starts at `diagram` and ends at
#   `child` — not just that the token parses.

#
# Redraw for the build-loop and sampling scout report (a restructure, not a local edit): new
# BUILD LOOP group (planner, builder, merger, held-out set, overseer) sits on the far left under
# the new ticket board, so MAP VIEW's frame stays one row wide and never covers CHAT PANE.
# accept sits left of state, fed by two lanes from tree and detail. tree->live runs over the
# top. child is 6 columns wide for its 5 south edges; the band under child is 5 rows so that
# gate->allow crosses child's south edges on one junction row. allow moved under runner. The
# old gate->allow (@werk-prefix) cells were removed; the new gate->allow is a different route.
#
# Redraw for #st-build-ticket (a restructure inside BUILD LOOP only): the single `builder` card
# is split into a nested BUILDER LOOP group of its four steps — implement, check, grade,
# review. implement is one column wide and 10 rows tall (rows 7-16), so its east face takes the
# forward edge to check plus the three "a new pass" back-edges, each on its own row, and its
# west face takes overseer and heldout. check is 2 rows tall so implement->check and
# check->implement each get their own row. check, grade, review stack in one column east of
# implement; merger sits under both, 9 columns wide, so review->merger, merger->implement and
# merger->heldout each leave its north face on a different column. merger->heldout is now a
# straight vertical hop (the old U-shape is gone). No junctions. The left block grew from 5 to
# 10 columns; every card and edge right of it (planner onward) moved 5 columns east, unchanged.
# overseer sits on implement's top row (7) on purpose: resolve.ts sizes a group frame from its
# DIRECT members only, so BUILD LOOP's frame does not grow to hold BUILDER LOOP's cards. With
# overseer on row 7 and merger on row 20, the outer frame covers the inner one anyway (the two
# frames share a top edge).
#
# Local edit for #ms-outcome-interv-chat: `flow` (the Flow tab) joins MAP VIEW at row 3, 1x2,
# in two new columns between `diagram` and the gate->approvebar lane. measure->asks runs down the
# east one and turns east at the asks row onto asks's west face. chatlog had no free face, so a
# new row under runner's fan makes chatlog (and child, log, planner, allow) 2 rows tall; measure->
# chatlog runs down the west column to a new bottom row, east along it, and back up to
# chatlog's new east face — a U-shaped detour. Junctions: both flow edges cross child->diagram,
# measure->chatlog also crosses cli->log, planner->cli and gate->allow.
#
# Local edit for #vi-sysdiag-quiet: `diagramsync` (the background job that runs the scout and
# the updater) joins SERVER PROCESS at row 21, in one new column east of child->diagram's
# column. `diagram` widens into that column, so diagramsync->diagram runs straight up it and
# crosses child->diagram's east turn on one junction. log->diagramsync leaves log's free west
# face, runs down beside it and east along row 21, crossing cli->log on one junction.
#
# Local edit for #vi-flow-localrate: two new edges into `pipelog`, which grows to 2 rows (22-23)
# so it has two free faces; implement->pipelog now ends on its west face. diagramsync->pipelog
# leaves diagramsync's south face and bends round its label onto pipelog's upper east face.
# flow widens by one new column (22, between measure->asks and the gate->approvebar lane);
# measure->pipelog runs down it, crosses child->diagram on one junction, turns west at row 24,
# crosses measure->asks and measure->chatlog on two junctions, and ends on pipelog's south face.
#
# Local edit for #st-ticket-watch: `ticketwatch` joins BUILD LOOP at row 7, in one new column
# (12) between planner->board's column and accept, so ticketwatch->board runs straight up it
# onto board's east face. log widens into a second new column (15, between accept->log and
# foldfn->log); log->ticketwatch leaves log's new free north face, runs up that column, crosses
# accept->log on one junction at row 9, and turns up into ticketwatch's south face.
#
# Local edit for #werk-board-build-subtree: two new edges, no new card. tree widens east into one
# new column (16, between log->ticketwatch's column and tree->state); tree->planner leaves tree's
# new free south face, runs down that column to row 13, turns west, crosses log->ticketwatch and
# accept->log on two junctions, and ends on planner's north face. planner widens to 2 columns
# (11-12), so planner->pipelog starts one cell east. planner->merger leaves planner's new south
# face, runs down column 12, crosses planner->cli on one junction at row 22, and ends on merger's
# south face.
#
# Local edit for #st-build-missing-decision: one new edge, no new card. cli widens east into one
# new column (between chatlog's column and measure->chatlog's column), so cli has a free south face.
# A new far-left column and a new bottom row carry implement->cli: it leaves implement's west
# face at row 16, crosses merger->board and implement->pipelog on two junctions, runs down the
# new left column, east along the new bottom row, and up the new column into cli's south face,
# crossing measure->chatlog on one junction at row 29.
#
# Restructure for #vi-flowtab: the old `flow` card splits in two. `measure` (the Measure tab)
# takes the old flow cells at row 3 and the three data-read edges, so every lane above that
# names measure->chatlog, measure->asks or measure->pipelog is unchanged in shape; the earlier
# comments that describe the `flow` card's cells and widening describe `measure` now. `flow`
# (the Flow tab, counts from the map cards only) sits in the free row 2 cells directly above
# measure, 3 columns wide.
#
# Local edit for #vi-flowtab-removed: one new edge, no new card. flow->accept leaves flow's north
# face, crosses tree->live on one junction, runs west along a new top row (its label in the
# middle), turns down column 15, crosses detail->accept on one junction, and ends on accept's
# north face. tree->accept moves one column east to make room: it leaves tree's west face, runs
# down column 16, and ends on accept's east face.
#
# Local edit for #werk-mc-bgagents: `bgline` (the background-agents line) joins CHAT PANE in the
# free row 4 cell east of `header`. It has no edges, so no lane changes.
#
# Local edit for #werk-mc-live-dead: `deadbar` (the attention bar) joins CHAT PANE in the
# free row 4 cell east of `bgline`. It has no edges, so no lane changes.
#
# Local edit for #st-build-ticket-hand-off: one new edge, no new card. Two new columns (8-9) sit
# between implement and its east lanes; every horizontal edge and card that spanned that gap
# (board, merger, the three "a new pass" back-edges, implement->check, implement->pipelog,
# implement->cli) grows by two cells. implement->board leaves implement's east face at row 10,
# runs up column 9, crosses implement->check and check->implement on two junctions, and ends on
# board's south face, its label at row 6. A column number above 7 in an earlier comment is now 2
# higher.
#
# Local edit for #werk-ci: `ci` joins TEST HARNESS, two columns wide, directly above unittest and
# e2e. Two new rows under live hold it (one empty row, then ci). ci->unittest and ci->e2e run
# straight down into the north faces of unittest and e2e. e2e->live moves off e2e's north face: a
# new column between e2e and runner carries it from e2e's east face up to live's south face. A
# row number above 8 or a column number above 31 in an earlier comment is now higher.
#
# Local edit for #werk-release and #werk-dist-channel: top-level `release` and `tap` sit east of
# ci, one row tall, on a new row 10 between live and ci. ci->release leaves ci's north face,
# crosses e2e->live and live->runner on two junctions, and ends on release's west face.
# release->tap runs straight east into tap. A row number above 9 in an earlier comment is now
# one higher.
#
# Local edit for #vi-flow-ms-tests: measure widens east by one new column (29). Column 29 in an
# earlier comment is now 30, and a column number above 29 there is now two higher. The edge that
# column carried (measure to unittest) is gone, and so is column 31's cell of it; measure keeps
# its fourth column.
#
# Local edit for #vi-jump, #vi-tabs and #werk-chat-image-inline: `search` and `viewtabs` join
# MAP VIEW in the free row 4 cells west of switcher. They have no edges. `attachments` joins
# STORE on a new east column (48), east of projectlist. live->attachments leaves live's south
# face at column 42, runs east along row 9, crosses switcher->projectlist on one junction, and
# runs down column 48 into attachments' north face. The image upload has no edge of its own: an
# edge id is its from->to pair, so it shares the composer->live edge and its label.
#
# Local edit for #vi-crumbs: `crumbs` joins MAP VIEW in the free cell of row 6, column 48, east
# of switcher, as the header shows it. It has no edges.
#
# Local edit for #ms-col-time: measure->board is a new edge. A new empty row 0 on top of the grid
# carries it. It leaves measure's north face at column 29, runs up that column, crosses
# tree->live on one junction, runs west along row 0, and runs down column 14 onto board's north
# face. Its label sits at row 0, column 21. A row number in an earlier comment is now one higher.
#
# Local edit for #ms-store-plan: runner->pipelog is a new edge. Two new rows (20-21) under
# runner's south fan lengthen runner->child, child->e2e and child->unittest, so row 20 can cross
# them. A new row (31) makes pipelog 3 rows tall and gives it a free east face. The edge leaves
# runner's south face at column 36, runs west along row 20 (junctions on runner->child,
# child->e2e, child->unittest, gate->approvebar), down column 29 (junction on child->diagram,
# label at row 27), and west along row 31 (junctions on measure->pipelog, measure->asks,
# measure->chatlog) onto pipelog's lowest east face. A row number above 19 in an earlier comment
# is now two higher, and above 28 three higher.
#
# Local edit for #werk-cli-followup: cli->board is a new edge. A new empty row 0 on top of the
# grid and a new empty east column (49) carry it. It leaves cli's north face at column 40, runs
# east along row 29, crosses measure->chatlog on one junction, runs up column 49, west along
# row 0, and down column 13 onto board's north face. Its label sits at row 0, column 30. A row
# number in an earlier comment is now one higher.

